  "history_of_present_illness": "The patient has experienced progressive chronic kidney disease over the past several years, advancing from stage 1 in 2017 to stage 4 by June 2025. Concurrent type 2 diabetes mellitus has manifested as proteinuria and microalbuminuria, contributing to renal decline. Hypertension has been difficult to control, requiring three antihypertensive agents. Anemia requiring epoetin alfa, osteoporosis treated with alendronate, and hypothyroidism on levothyroxine are also present. Lifestyle factors\u2014including daily tobacco use, unhealthy alcohol consumption, and ongoing intimate partner abuse\u2014add to cardiovascular and renal risk. The patient is currently awaiting a kidney transplant and remains employed full\u2011time. Recent labs and vital signs are missing, and the recorded HbA1c of 2.9% is likely erroneous.",
